                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_420">Oxford,
                                Oxfordshire, Franciscan convent</orgName>
                            <p>This attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval
                                Libraries of Great Britain (1964), which did not change in the
                                Supplement (1987). The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great
                                Britain index card originally noted the following: 'full of notes in
                                the hand of Grosseteste, who bequeathed his books to the
                                Franciscans'. However, Ker later added a query to the card, writing:
                                'but this is discredited by S. Harrison Thomson, <title>Writing of
                                    Robert Grosseteste</title> (1940), p. 30, who says that none of
                                the marginalia are in his hand.'</p></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">On last page is <persName>John
                                Farley's</persName> name, written in Greek letters.</provenance>
                    </history>
